<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">12 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 12 December, from 627 to 2000.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">627 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,399 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Heraclius defeats the Persians near Nineveh</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius">Heraclius</a> routed a Sasanian army near the ruins of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nineveh">Nineveh</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>. The victory ended a 26-year war, but both exhausted empires soon fell prey to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/early-muslim-conquests">Arab conquests</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius">Heraclius</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nineveh">Nineveh</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/newfoundland.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1901 CE <span class="tih-ago">125 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Marconi receives the first transatlantic radio signal</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Signal Hill in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guglielmo-marconi">Guglielmo Marconi</a> heard the Morse letter 'S' sent from Poldhu in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cornwall">Cornwall</a>, some 3,500 kilometres away. The feat showed that radio could span oceans.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1911 CE <span class="tih-ago">115 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George V announces the move of India's capital to Delhi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-durbar">Delhi Durbar</a>, attended by hundreds of thousands, King-Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-v">George V</a> announced that the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a> would move from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kolkata">Calcutta</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-delhi">New Delhi</a> was inaugurated in 1931.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1963 CE <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Kenya gains independence with Jomo Kenyatta as prime minister</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Kenya became independent from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jomo-kenyatta">Jomo Kenyatta</a>, jailed by the colonial authorities during the Mau Mau emergency, became prime minister and later the country's first president.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">2000 CE <span class="tih-ago">26 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Supreme Court halts the Florida recount in Bush v. Gore</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">By five votes to four, the US Supreme Court stopped the manual recount of presidential votes in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>. The ruling left George W. Bush the winner of Florida, and of the presidency, by 537 votes.</p></div></li></ol>
